--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party software
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

None. The application is a single HTML file built from the sources in this
repository: HTML and CSS written for this project, a translation table with
four locales, a small geometry engine and about 900 lines of plain
JavaScript. It bundles no library, no framework, no analytics and no font
file, and it loads nothing from the network at runtime - not even a CDN copy
of anything.

The PNG density writer (a pHYs chunk inserted after IHDR, with a CRC-32 over
the chunk type and data) is implemented in this project from the public PNG
specification, RFC 2083. It does not include code from libpng, zlib or any
other encoder.

The photo standards used for the guides (ICAO Doc 9303, the EU Visa Code and
the United States Department of State guidance) are published specifications.
Only the numbers are used here; no document, image or template from those
publishers is redistributed.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
External services
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

None. The photo is decoded from a local file inside the browser, cropped on a
canvas and handed back as a download or a print job. No photo, no filename and
no metadata ever leaves the device, which also means there is no server-side
storage, no account and no upload limit other than the memory of the browser.
